es remain on disk. `restart_process` skips file transfers by checking `dest.exists()` and utilizing a new `is_restart` boolean flag in `_process_worker` to safely re-trigger the extraction pipeline.\n- **Frontend Tab State**: `switchScreen` in JS uses `display: none` to hide inactive screens. Placing `#progress-modal` inside `#screen-new` elegantly leverages the DOM state to persist the loading UI without needing complex global state management in JS.\n- **Extraction Fallback Flow**: `pdf_reader.py` attempts extraction in this order: `_try_extracted_data` -> `_try_html_tables` -> (NEW) `_extract_with_gemini` -> (NEW relaxed) `_try_text_content`. The Gemini fallback depends on `gemini_api_key` being passed into `extract_items_from_pdf`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Files and Code\n\n### Edited Files\n- **`d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\desktop_app\\templates\\index.html`**\n  - *What:* Refactored `#progress-modal` CSS to an absolute overlay. Fixed JS ternary logic for history action buttons (processing = disabled spinner; error = restart/delete). Added `restartProcess` JS function.\n  - *Why:* To fulfill UX placement requests and support the new restart feature.\n- **`d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\desktop_app\\backend.py`**\n  - *What:* Added `restart_process` endpoint. Updated `_process_worker` to accept `is_restart` and ignore `shutil.copy2` if files already exist.\n  - *Why:* To allow users to retry stuck/failed processes from the history tab.\n- **`d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\src\\extract\\pdf_reader.py`**\n  - *What:* Added `gemini_api_key` parameter to `parse_items_from_response` and `extract_items_from_pdf`. Implemented `_extract_with_gemini` using `google.genai`. Removed element type restrictions from `_try_text_content`.\n  - *Why:* Unstructured API was struggling to reliably format tables from the user's varied PDFs, resulting in 0 extracted items. Gemini serves as a highly robust fallback.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n\n**Current Status:** The restart capability and tab-scoped loading overlay are implemented. The Gemini API fallback is written in `pdf_reader.py` but needs to be fully wired up from the configuration root.\n\n**Immediate Next Steps:**\n1. **Wire up Gemini Key:** Open `d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\src\\extract\\file_handler.py`. Ensure that `gemini_api_key` from `config` is being passed into the `extract_items_from_pdf` call. Currently, it might only be passing the Unstructured key.\n2. **Implement System Logs UI:** Open `d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\desktop_app\\templates\\index.html`. Focus on the `#screen-settings` section. Add a button/toggle (e.g., \"عرض سجل النظام\") that expands a terminal box containing system logs, ensuring it takes up the main content area exactly as the user requested.\n3. **Verify:** Run the app (`python run_app.py`) and verify that a failed process can be restarted from the History tab, and that PDF extraction utilizes the Gemini fallback when standard parsing fails.\n\nYou have the 23 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: agent]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.agents/agents/desktop-builder/agent.md\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T22:17:02Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: agent]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.agents/agents/pharmacy-builder/agent.md\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T10:46:04Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1790006220414]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.user_uploaded/media_1790006220414.png\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T15:57:26Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1790006245677]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.user_uploaded/media_1790006245677.png\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T15:57:26Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1790008142552]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.user_uploaded/media_17900081